{%- doc -%}
  Renders an outline SVG map of a coffee's origin country, from a plain country name.

  Usage: {% render 'country-map', country: product.metafields.custom.country.value %}
  (or pass any country string). Outputs nothing when the country is blank or has no map
  on file, so a caller can test the captured output and hide its wrapper when empty.

  The stroke is `currentColor`, so the colour comes from the surrounding element -- set
  `color` on the parent to theme it. Maps are inline so the stroke stays crisp and themeable.

  Adding a country: add a `when` below with the country's lower-cased, hyphenated name and
  its SVG. Source outlines: mapsicon (github.com/djaiss/mapsicon), traced with potrace; the
  transform/viewBox are kept and only the paint is overridden to a non-scaling stroke.
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  # `country` arrives as a render argument, which theme-check cannot see.
  # theme-check-disable UndefinedObject
  assign h = country | strip | downcase | replace: '.', '' | replace: ',', '' | replace: '  ', ' ' | replace: ' ', '-'
  # theme-check-enable UndefinedObject
  # Common aliases -> canonical handle
  case h
    when 'drc', 'dr-congo', 'congo', 'democratic-republic-of-the-congo'
      assign h = 'democratic-republic-of-the-congo'
    when 'usa', 'united-states-of-america'
      assign h = 'united-states'
  endcase
-%}
